  "question": {
    "text": "Liquids A and B form ideal solution over the entire range of composition. At temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>, equimolar binary solution of liquids A and B has vapour pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> . At the same temperature, a new solution of A and B having mole fractions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>and</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></math>, respectively, has vapour pressure of <math><mn>22.5</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac></math>, in the new solution is ____.<br />(Given that the vapour pressure of pure liquid A is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Torr</mi></math>&nbsp;at temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "19",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msubsup><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msubsup><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn></math> .... <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math><br />Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>Torr</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>Torr</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>.5</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>torr</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>70</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></math>.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>70</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>.5</mo></mrow><mn>50</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.95</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.05</mo></math><br />So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.95</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.05</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>19</mn></math>.",
